// === NAME - DESCRIPTION: Sampling Distribution of the Sum - Probability P(Sigma x > c) ===
// === SET QUESTION TYPE TO: multipart ===

// === COMMON CONTROL ===
loadlibrary("stats");

// Population parameters
$popMean = rand(10, 30);
$popStdDev = rand(3, 8);

// Sample size (n) - keep it large enough for CLT to be reasonable
$n = rand(30, 60);

// Target sum (c)
// Expected sum is $n * $popMean.
$sumStdDev = $popStdDev * sqrt($n);
$sumMean = $n * $popMean;

// Randomly pick a target sum c that is within +/- 2 standard deviations of the mean sum
$offset = (rand(-200, 200) / 100) * $sumStdDev;
$c = round($sumMean + $offset, 2);

// Calculations for the key
// Z = (c - n*mu) / (sigma * sqrt(n))
$zScore = ($c - $sumMean) / $sumStdDev;

// normalcdf(z) in the stats library returns P(Z < z).
// P(Sum > c) = P(Z > zScore) = 1 - P(Z < zScore)
$prob = 1 - normalcdf($zScore);

// Parts
$anstypes = "number,number,number";

// Part 0: Expected value of the sum
$answer[0] = $sumMean;

// Part 1: Standard deviation of the sum
$answer[1] = round($sumStdDev, 4);

// Part 2: Probability
$answer[2] = round($prob, 4);

// Formatting for display
$popMeanDisp = round($popMean, 2);
$popStdDevDisp = round($popStdDev, 2);
$nDisp = $n;
$cDisp = $c;

// Build the solution guide with backticks for MathJax rendering
$sg0 = '1. By the Central Limit Theorem, the expected value of the sum of ' . $nDisp . ' observations is: `E(\Sigma x) = n \cdot \mu = ' . $nDisp . ' \cdot ' . $popMeanDisp . ' = ' . $sumMean . '`';
$sg1 = '2. The standard deviation of the sum is: `\sigma_{\Sigma x} = \sqrt{n} \cdot \sigma = \sqrt{' . $nDisp . '} \cdot ' . $popStdDevDisp . ' \approx ' . round($sumStdDev, 4) . '`';
$sg2 = '3. To find the probability that the sum is greater than ' . $cDisp . ', we calculate the z-score: `z = \frac{c - E(\Sigma x)}{\sigma_{\Sigma x}} = \frac{' . $cDisp . ' - ' . $sumMean . '}{' . round($sumStdDev, 4) . '} \approx ' . round($zScore, 4) . '`';
$sg3 = '4. Using the standard normal distribution: `P(\Sigma x > ' . $cDisp . ') = P(Z > ' . round($zScore, 4) . ') = 1 - P(Z < ' . round($zScore, 4) . ') \approx ' . round($prob, 4) . '`';

$solutionguide = $sg0 . "\n\n" . $sg1 . "\n\n" . $sg2 . "\n\n" . $sg3;

// === QUESTION TEXT ===
A population has a mean of `$popMeanDisp` and a standard deviation of `$popStdDevDisp`. 
A random sample of size `$nDisp` is selected from this population.

<p>Assuming the sample size is large enough to apply the Central Limit Theorem:</p>

<p>a) What is the expected value of the sum of the observations in the sample?
`E(\Sigma x) =` $answerbox[0]</p>

<p>b) What is the standard deviation of the sum of the observations in the sample? 
(Round your answer to four decimal places)
`\sigma_{\Sigma x} =` $answerbox[1]</p>

<p>c) What is the probability that the sum of the observations in the sample is greater than `$cDisp`? 
(Round your answer to four decimal places)
`P(\Sigma x > $cDisp) =` $answerbox[2]</p>

// === NAME - DESCRIPTION: Combinations With Condition - Count committees from a group, then count those including a specific member ===
// === SET QUESTION TYPE TO: multipart ===

// === COMMON CONTROL ===
# Total group size
$n = rand(8, 12);
# Committee size
$k = rand(3, 5);

# Ensure k < n
if ($k >= $n) {
    $n = $k + 3;
}

# Randomize names for the group
$allNames = array(
    "Alice", "Bob", "Charlie", "Diana", "Edward", "Fiona", "George", "Hannah", 
    "Ian", "Julia", "Kevin", "Laura"
);
$selectedNames = diffrandsfrom($allNames, $n);

# Pick one specific person to be the "required" member
$targetIdx = rand(0, $n - 1);
$targetPerson = $selectedNames[$targetIdx];

# Calculate nCk = (n * (n-1) * ... * (n-k+1)) / k!
# Part 1: Total combinations nCk
$num0 = 1;
for ($i = 0; $i < $k; $i++) {
    $num0 *= ($n - $i);
}
$den0 = 1;
for ($i = 1; $i <= $k; $i++) {
    $den0 *= $i;
}
$ans0 = $num0 / $den0;

# Part 2: Combinations including the specific person
# Choose k-1 more from the remaining n-1
$k_prime = $k - 1;
$n_prime = $n - 1;

$num1 = 1;
for ($i = 0; $i < $k_prime; $i++) {
    $num1 *= ($n_prime - $i);
}
$den1 = 1;
for ($i = 1; $i <= $k_prime; $i++) {
    $den1 *= $i;
}
$ans1 = $num1 / $den1;

$answer = array($ans0, $ans1);
$anstypes = "number,number";

# Formatting the list of names for the prompt
$nameList = arraytolist($selectedNames, ", ");

// === QUESTION TEXT ===
A committee of {$k} people is to be formed from the following group of {$n} people: 
{$nameList}.

<p>a) How many different committees can be formed?
<br>Answer: $answerbox[0]</p>

<p>b) How many of these committees include {$targetPerson}?
<br>Answer: $answerbox[1]</p>

// === ANSWER ===
$solutionguide = "Part (a): The number of ways to choose a committee of {$k} people from a group of {$n} is given by the combination formula nCk: 
`C({$n}, {$k}) = {$n}! / ({$k}!({$n}-{$k})!) = {$ans0}`.

Part (b): If {$targetPerson} is on the committee, we have already filled 1 spot. We need to choose the remaining " . ($k - 1) . " members from the remaining " . ($n - 1) . " people:
`C(" . ($n - 1) . ", " . ($k - 1) . ") = " . ($n - 1) . "! / (" . ($k - 1) . "!(" . ($n - 1) . "-" . ($k - 1) . ")!) = {$ans1}`.";

